To find out how many mosaic tiles Mr. Boarden needs to cover two-thirds of his bathroom, we can follow these steps:

1. **Calculate the area to be covered**: Mr. Boarden needs to cover two-thirds of his 36 square feet bathroom. So, we calculate:
   \[
   \text{Area to be covered} = \frac{2}{3} \times 36 \text{ square feet}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Area to be covered} = 24 \text{ square feet}
   \]

2. **Calculate the number of tiles needed**: Mr. Boarden needs 24 tiles for every square foot. So, we calculate:
   \[
   \text{Number of tiles needed} = 24 \text{ tiles/square foot} \times 24 \text{ square feet}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Number of tiles needed} = 576 \text{ tiles}
   \]

Therefore, Mr. Boarden would need 576 mosaic tiles to cover two-thirds of his 36 square feet bathroom. {reasoning process} #### {576}
